; HomerView.jkm -- HomerView key map for Microsoft Edge
;
; Loaded with HomerView.jsb whenever Edge has focus.
;
; What is deliberately absent matters as much as what is here. JAWS already
; moves to a declared main region with Q, says the web address with JAWSKey+A,
; lists headings, links and form fields with JAWSKey+F5, F6 and F7, says the
; title with JAWSKey+T, and finds with Control+F and F3. HomerView on NVDA has
; its own versions of all of those, and only because NVDA lacks them. Binding
; them here would take keys a JAWS user already knows and give them something
; almost, but not quite, the same. That is worse than adding nothing.
;
; So this binds the commands JAWS does not have, and one that fills the gap Q
; leaves.
;
; Modifiers are written in alphabetical order, which is the Homer convention:
; Alt, Control, JAWSKey, Shift.

[Common Keys]

; -----------------------------------------------------------------
; Shift+Q. About half the web declares no main region at all, and on
; those pages Q has nothing to move to. This weighs every part of the
; page, the most text with the fewest links winning, and says that it
; inferred the answer rather than being told it. On a page that does
; declare one, it says so and sends you to Q.
; -----------------------------------------------------------------
Shift+Q=moveToProbableMain

; -----------------------------------------------------------------
; The commands nothing else has. All of these ask the browser
; something a reading order cannot answer.
; -----------------------------------------------------------------
Alt+JAWSKey+E=explorePage
Alt+JAWSKey+A=checkAccessibility
Alt+L=describeLinkTarget
Shift+F9=extractMainContent

[Keyboard Layouts]
Desktop=Common
Laptop=Common
